From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 01:25:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add scalar overloads for World/WorldBorder box queries

Give the block/material queries that only read a box's bounds an overload
taking the six doubles directly (checkBlockCollision, containsLiquid,
isFlammableWithin, handleMaterialAcceleration, isMaterialInBB,
isAABBInMaterial, WorldBorder.contains). The existing AxisAlignedBB
signatures stay as thin delegates, so nothing changes yet.

This is the groundwork for removing AxisAlignedBB: once callers hold
their bounds as doubles they can query the world without building a box
just to be read apart again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

